@startuml bag-exhausting-removal-diagnosis
' ============================================================================
' Bug 14492 (PathMap journal J-259): where the RhoSpec time went, and the fix.
'   BLUE   #1565C0  the RSpace callers of a datum removal
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  the pending-delta cancellation and the Bag removal
'   RED    #C62828  the work that grows with the Bag: rebuild and drain
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  the in-place removal of stack-safety report section 5.60.7
' Counts are on-CPU stack samples of one release run of system_vault_spec,
' taken every 3 s (57 in all). M is the Bag's number of distinct endpoints
' and k the removed key.
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #455A64
  ParticipantBorderColor #455A64
  GroupBorderColor #455A64
  DividerBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
}

title <b>Bug 14492: an exhausting cancellation rebuilt and drained the whole Bag</b>\n57 on-CPU samples of a release ""system_vault_spec"" run, one every 3 s

participant "locked_produce" as Produce #BBDEFB
participant "HotStore::\napply_accepted_match" as Accept #BBDEFB
participant "RSpaceDataStore::\nremove_path" as Store #BBDEFB
participant "BagDelta::\nrecord_change" as Delta #FFE0B2
participant "Bag::\ntry_remove_many" as Remove #FFE0B2
participant "Bag::subtract\n(try_from_sorted_unique)" as Rebuild #FFCDD2
participant "AnchorRoot::drop\n(drain_pathmap)" as Drain #FFCDD2

== before the fix: tree d98fed8cd (arm A) ==
Produce -[#1565C0]> Accept : an accepted COMM
Accept -[#1565C0]> Store : remove each consumed datum
note right of Store #E3F2FD
  42 stacks reach ""try_remove_many"":
  35 through this chain and
  7 through the pending loop
  of ""RSpaceDataStore::apply_delta""
end note
Store -[#EF6C00]> Delta : record the removal in the pending delta
Delta -[#EF6C00]> Remove : cancel a pending addition
Remove -[#C62828]> Rebuild : the count reaches 0:\n""*self = self.subtract(&removal)""
Rebuild --[#C62828]> Remove : a fresh Bag, <latex>\Theta(M)</latex>
Remove -[#C62828]> Drain : drop the replaced anchor
Drain --[#C62828]> Remove : the old trie drained, <latex>\Theta(M)</latex>
note over Rebuild, Drain #FFEBEE
  52 of 57 samples (91%) are inside ""AnchorRoot::drop"":
  32 in Phase A and 20 in Phase B. Their triggers:
  41 ""try_remove_many"" rebuilds, 5 value-free donors,
  5 ""ChannelSlot"" maps and 1 ""Par"".
  3 more samples are in Bag rebuild frames.
end note

== after the fix: stack-safety report 5.60.7 ==
Produce -[#1565C0]> Accept : an accepted COMM
Accept -[#1565C0]> Store : remove each consumed datum
Store -[#EF6C00]> Delta : record the removal in the pending delta
Delta -[#EF6C00]> Remove : cancel a pending addition
alt exclusive anchor: one wrapper and the flag set
  Remove -[#2E7D32]> Remove : prune <latex>k</latex> in place:\n<latex>O(|k|)</latex> work, <latex>O(1)</latex> stack
else shared anchor: at most once per Bag per soft checkpoint
  Remove -[#C62828]> Rebuild : the rebuild, as before
  Rebuild --[#C62828]> Remove : a fresh exclusive Bag
end
@enduml
